<!-- SECTION 6: THE BIRTHDAY -->
<h2>July 13 — The Birthday on the Eve of the Semifinals</h2>
<p>Yamal turns 19 on July 13, 2026. The World Cup semifinals are scheduled for July 14 and 15. If Spain advance through their bracket, Yamal will celebrate his 19th birthday during the World Cup semifinals — the most high-stakes stage of the biggest tournament in sports.</p>
<p>If Spain win the whole thing on July 19, Yamal will be 19 years and 6 days old at the final whistle — younger than Pelé was when he won the 1958 World Cup at 17 years old? No. Pelé was 17 at that final. But Yamal would be the youngest player to win a World Cup since Pelé — and the youngest player to win it in the tournament's expanded 48-team format, which did not exist when Pelé was playing.</p>
<p>When the 2007 UNICEF photograph was taken — Messi bathing a six-month-old Yamal — nobody in that room was thinking about World Cups. Messi was 20 years old, already playing for Barcelona, not yet the player he would become. Yamal was six months old and, by all available evidence, probably asleep shortly after. Eighteen years later, they are both at the same tournament, both scoring goals. One has broken every record the sport has. The other is 18 and has just started breaking them.</p>
